\ Nested interrupt tests, RV QEMU only.
\ Outer: faux SysTick (slot 7 -> systick# 15). Inner: msip (slot 3).

TESTING nested interrupts (RV): msip inside the SysTick handler

-int
-systick
0 msip !

variable old.tick  systick# trap@ old.tick !
variable outer  variable inner  variable inside  variable seen
variable odepth  variable idepth  variable orp  variable irp
variable rp0

: rv.clear  0 outer ! 0 inner ! 0 inside ! 0 seen !
   0 odepth ! 0 idepth ! 0 orp ! 0 irp ! ;
rv.clear

\ inner: clear the source, record depth, RS and whether outer is active
:noname  0 msip !  1 inner +!  in-isr? @ idepth !
   rp@ irp !  inside @ seen ! ;i  3 trap!
3 irq.on

\ outer: allow nesting, raise msip, then leave (no -int: (exiti) masks)
:noname  1 outer +!  in-isr? @ odepth !  rp@ orp !
   1 inside !  +int  1 msip !  0 inside ! ;i  systick# trap!

rp@ rp0 !
systick.ms 1- systick!
+systick
+int
T{ 20 ms  inner @ 0>  ->  true }T
-int

\ inner ran while outer was inside
T{ seen @  ->  1 }T
\ in-isr? counts the nesting
T{ odepth @ idepth @  ->  1 2 }T
\ inner RS below outer RS
T{ irp @ orp @ u<  ->  true }T
\ outer RS below the task RS
T{ orp @ rp0 @ u<  ->  true }T
\ task RS balanced
T{ rp@ rp0 @ =  ->  true }T
\ all handlers gone
T{ in-isr? @  ->  0 }T
\ one inner per outer
T{ inner @ outer @ - abs 2 <  ->  true }T

TESTING no nesting without +int in the handler

-systick
0 msip !
rv.clear

:noname  1 outer +!  1 inside !  1 msip !
   0 inside ! ;i  systick# trap!

+systick
+int
T{ 20 ms  inner @ 0>  ->  true }T
-int
\ inner ran only after outer returned
T{ seen @ idepth @  ->  0 1 }T

\ CLEANUP
-systick
0 msip !
3 irq.off
3 trap-
systick.max
: rv.restore  old.tick @ ?dup
   if systick# trap! else systick# trap- then ;
rv.restore
+systick
